# Intergalactic Teacher - Interactive Reading Platform

## Project Overview
Educational web app creating personalized AI-powered stories for children 7-12 years old.
Supports Hebrew and English with real-time streaming story generation.

## Tech Stack
- Backend: FastAPI, Python 3.11+, PostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy, LangGraph, Ollama
- Frontend: React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Zustand
- Streaming: Server-Sent Events (SSE) for real-time content delivery

## Key Architecture Patterns
- Clean architecture: controllers → services → repositories → models
- Streaming workflows using LangGraph with .astream_events()
- JWT authentication with child profile access control
- Type-safe APIs with Pydantic models

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript strict mode everywhere
- Async functions for all I/O operations
- Comprehensive error handling with structured logging
- SSE events must follow the format in `backend/app/utils/sse_formatter.py`
- Frontend state management via Zustand stores
- Component props should be properly typed interfaces

## Current Focus Areas
- Implementing token streaming for story generation
- Building ChatGPT-like conversational interface
- Ensuring child safety with content filtering
- Performance optimization for concurrent users

## Testing Requirements
- Unit tests for all service methods
- Integration tests for streaming workflows
- E2E tests for complete user journeys
- Performance tests for story generation speed

## File Naming Conventions
- React components: PascalCase (e.g., `StoryCard.tsx`)
- Services: camelCase (e.g., `storyService.ts`)
- Types: PascalCase interfaces (e.g., `interface StoryState`)
- API endpoints: snake_case (e.g., `/api/v1/stories/generate`)
- Database models: PascalCase classes (e.g., `class Story`)

## Important Notes
- Always validate child access permissions before story operations
- Use structured logging with context (child_id, session_id, etc.)
- Implement proper error boundaries in React components
- Follow COPPA compliance guidelines for child data protection
- Test Hebrew text rendering and RTL support thoroughly

## Streaming Implementation Guidelines
- Use SSE (Server-Sent Events) for real-time content delivery
- Follow the event format: `{type, data}` structure
- Handle connection errors gracefully with retry logic
- Implement proper cleanup on component unmount
- Use EventSource API on frontend for SSE consumption

## Security Guidelines
- Validate all user inputs, especially for children's safety
- Implement content filtering at multiple levels
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection
- Store JWT tokens securely and implement proper refresh logic
- Log security events for monitoring and audit trails

## GitHub Project Management
- **Repository**: https://github.com/niros1/intergalactic-teacher
- **Project Board**: https://github.com/users/niros1/projects/2

### Issue Management Guidelines
- **For NEW work** (features, bugs, improvements): Create a GitHub issue and link it to the project board
- **For EXISTING issues**: Work directly on the existing issue - do NOT create a new one
- All issues should be properly categorized with appropriate labels
- Link issues to the project board for tracking and organization
- Include clear descriptions, acceptance criteria, and technical details in issues
- Reference related issues and pull requests for better traceability

### When Creating New Issues
- Provide clear, descriptive titles
- Include detailed descriptions with context and requirements
- Add appropriate labels (feature, bug, enhancement, etc.)
- Set priority levels when applicable
- Link to the project board for tracking
- Include technical specifications and implementation notes when relevant

### When Start working on issue
- Open a new branch with the issue number and issue title
